{:part "III"
 :claim "Once the rewriting operator becomes per-cell, neighbour-transmitted state, the lattice realises all three outcomes (live wins, frozen wins, coexistence) separated by a bisectable boundary in precision, but no tested locally computable quantity can find or hold the coexistence, and the absorbing frozen endpoints are created by the adoption policy at high precision, not by the lattice underneath."
 :sections
 [{:title "Exotypes (part opening)" :label "part:endogenous"
   :claim "The part's move is that the operator becomes a property of the cell, and its four findings are: three outcomes at the tested parameters, no local quantity finds the third, the protective intervention backfires while noise merely prevents freezing, and the frozen endpoints are an effect of the adoption rule."
   :title-matches-claim false
   :paragraphs
   [{:n 1 :opening "In Part~II the gain of the phenotype-to-genotype"
     :role :transition
     :note "Hands off from Part II's reading gate (firing endogenous, operator still run-level) to the part's move: operator becomes per-cell; correct and sufficient."}
    {:n 2 :opening "Its findings, in order. When the operator"
     :role :states-claim
     :note "Findings roadmap in discovery order; internally consistent with the sections (thirty control runs = 6 + 24), but one clause overclaims relative to the closure section's hedge (see violations)."}]
   :violations
   [{:quote "the changing phase eliminates the frozen phase"
     :kind :opaque-compression
     :suggest "frozen/live is defined only in the Three Outcomes section (fifteen-step criterion); at this first use add a half-clause gloss, e.g. 'the changing phase (regions still updating) eliminates the frozen phase (regions whose phenotypes have stopped changing)'."}
    {:quote "reproducing the found configuration's structure"
     :kind :scope-creep
     :suggest "The closure section twice declines exactly this claim ('Whether that state differs from the valley configuration in structure is not settled by the statistics we computed'; 'the uncontrolled state has not been shown to match the found configuration in structure'). Align the summary with the hedge: e.g. 'prevents freezing while holding a far higher frozen fraction than the found configuration' (whether the structure matches is stated as unsettled)."}]}

