   :claim "The exotype is a per-cell propagator assignment whose transition is the familiar elementary write of Part I applied one coordinate at a time, making it a structured (address-biased), always-on, heritable mutation operator, with a twelve-member vocabulary exactly audited by the Part I theorem."
   :title-matches-claim true
   :paragraphs
   [{:n 1 :opening "An exotype is a per-cell assignment of"
     :role :machinery
     :note "Defines the exotype; correctly isolates what is new (the assignment) from what is not (the operator family)."}
    {:n 2 :opening "The transition is one elementary write. At"
     :role :machinery
     :note "The write equation plus its continuity with sec:object and Part I's spatial experiments; needed for every result downstream."}
    {:n 3 :opening "Three properties matter for what follows. The"
     :role :evidence
     :note "Argues the title's claim directly: structured (read/write addresses differ), ordinary-path (fires every step), heritable (persists and transmits) -- the Baldwin hook."}
    {:n 4 :opening "The implemented vocabulary is twelve named members"
